      "question": {
        ":question/id": "1c165030-6920-5600-9915-e7a3de47595e",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =-1\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
